## 3. How Module Access Auto-Populates

When HR creates an employee and checks modules:

```
module_access row is created/updated
    │
    ├─ task_manager = TRUE
    │     └─ Employee can see/access Task Manager in navbar
    │        (Task Manager reads module_access to show members)
    │
    ├─ auditing = TRUE
    │     └─ Employee can see/access Auditing in navbar
    │        (Auditing project assignment still manual by Audit Lead)
    │
    └─ crm = TRUE
          └─ Employee can see/access CRM in navbar
```

No separate member tables needed. The `module_access` table IS the single source of truth for who can access what. Each module queries `module_access` to filter its own data.

